  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Inclusive and Sustainable Peace in the Andriry Massif</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to build upon the achievements of the Peacebuilding Fund (PBF) interventions in the Andriry mountain region in southern Madagascar, extending its reach to more remote, marginalized, and conflict-prone communities. Since 2017, holistic support has been provided to restore security, enhance social cohesion, and promote peaceful coexistence in the area through PBF funding. While the PBF interventions have made significant progress, particularly around the Andriry mountain, the more secluded and inaccessible interior of the massif remains a refuge enclave where state services struggle to reach. To address this, the project focuses on inclusivity, aiming to engage marginalized communities within the massif, fostering social cohesion and sustainable development. The project&apos;s ambitions include strengthening social cohesion through community participation in peace processes, improving access to peace dividends for Andriry communities, and establishing a coordination mechanism for sustainable development and peace promotion in the region. The initiative aligns with broader efforts by the government and development partners to invest in the area&apos;s development, leveraging previous PBF investments and contributing to a more coordinated &quot;Humanitarian-Development-Peace&quot; (HDP) approach.</narrative>
  </description>
